{
  "$comment": "The six default design systems, one folder each — static content served verbatim from public/. Fields path/thumbnail/readme/theme are relative to this directory; the app serves it under its base path (/design/design-systems/ as deployed). Each system's files array lists every file in its folder, folder-relative (fetch from path + files[i].path), with binary:true on non-text assets — so a client can copy a whole system from one manifest read. One exception: the committed preview image named by thumbnailImage lives in the folder but stays OUT of files — it seeds the picked project's server-side thumbnail slot and must not be copied into the project (it is also a render artifact: re-render it from thumbnail.html after restyling a system). A client can read this file instead of globbing the directory.",
